istency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.16381514257620453,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.07287631311642227,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":9.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.09259540391430525,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.032818020918720325,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":9.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.01501556491485076,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":75.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.18921,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Flutter Entertainment plc operates as a sports betting and gaming company in the United States, the United Kingdom, Ireland, Australia, Italy, and internationally. It provides sportsbooks; iGaming products, such as blackjack, roulette, slot machines, poker, and rummy, as well as lottery products; and sports betting products, which include Betfair betting exchanges, daily fantasy sports, and horse racing wagering under the TVG brand. The company offers sports betting and gaming services through fanduel.com, tvg.com, betfair.com, paddypower.com, and paddypower.ie, sportsbet.com.au, pokerstars.com, betfair.com, sisal.it, maxbet.rs, and adjarabet.com websites under the FanDuel, Sky Betting & Gaming, Sportsbet, PokerStars, Paddy Power, Sisal, tombola, Betfair, TVG, Adjarabet, and MaxBet brands, as well as live poker tours and events. It also provides business-to-business pricing and risk management services. The company was formerly known as Paddy Power Betfair plc and changed its name to Flutter Entertainment plc in 2019. Flutter Entertainment plc was incorporated in 1958 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel Mark Taylor | Group CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 28K people. Revenue per employee of $574K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $38K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Flutter Entertainment plc is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $12.4B market cap on $16.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are contracting by -6.0pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 46%.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -6.0pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 54% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 39% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3875423031189975},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 24% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Flutter Entertainment (FLUT) On Tax Hits And Buyb